  "worked_solution": "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(10,0,-6)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=\u27e83,-7,-5\u27e9.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{3}=\\frac{y-0}{-7}=\\frac{z-(-6)}{-5}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{3}=\\frac{y}{-7}=\\frac{z+6}{-5}.\n$$",
